\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {7.10}{\ignorespaces Verification status of critical claims. ``Method'' is the formal technique; ``Result'' is its outcome; ``Artifact'' names the public bundle file. A claim with both a formal artifact \emph  {and} a runtime conformance test is fully closed ({\leavevmode {\color  {hhink}\textsc  {\textbf  {closed}}}}); a claim with formal model but no deployed runtime is spec-only ({\leavevmode {\color  {hhgray}\textit  {spec-only}}}); a claim with empirical evidence but no formal mechanization is partial ({\leavevmode {\color  {hhink}\textsc  {partial}}}).\relax }}{505}{table.7.appendix.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{bonded:tab:verification-status}{{7.10}{505}{Verification status of critical claims. ``Method'' is the formal technique; ``Result'' is its outcome; ``Artifact'' names the public bundle file. A claim with both a formal artifact \emph {and} a runtime conformance test is fully closed (\Closed ); a claim with formal model but no deployed runtime is spec-only (\SpecOnly ); a claim with empirical evidence but no formal mechanization is partial (\Partial ).\relax }{table.7.appendix.10}{}}
